0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Intel 8080
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-21).
0000                             ;  Design follows the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm), with 8080 opcodes
0000                             ;  only.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Two switches, set in the two EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), I8080 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the 8080"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The return stack pointer has no register (the 8080 has no spare pair): it
0000                             ;  is the RAM word RSP. Only rpop, rpushd and ")" (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three. (asm80 wants the vector number: RST 1 = RST 08h.)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 1  08h  rpop    pop the return stack into HL
0000                             ;    RST 3  18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 4  20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 5  28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 6  30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 3 and RST 6 never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing each
0000                             ;  of them does is POP D to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block has no jumps inside itself, so it works at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  What the 8080 lacks, and what replaces it: no JR (JMP/Jcc), no DJNZ, no
0000                             ;  SBC HL (byte-wise SUB/SBB, or negate and DAD), no shifts on register pairs
0000                             ;  (DAD H doubles; RAL/RAR through A), no LDIR/CPIR (small loops).
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
                    BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
                    BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
0000                             ;   (end the routine with ORA A / RET).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE and HL.
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSP:      EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: the return stack pointer;
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+36h   ;   a held-back key;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_'
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                          .ORG   BASE   
0000                          IF   1-(1-CPM)*CHECKED   
                              LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0000                          ENDIF      
0000   C3 C7 04               JMP   start   ; In the checked generic build this is at 0000h
0003                             ;   (and `start` sets SP): its first byte, C3h,
0003                             ;   is what an undefined word runs into, as
0003                             ;   CP/M's own JMP at 0000h is in a .COM: e_hi.
0003                          IF   (1-CPM)*CHECKED   
0003   00 00 00               DB   0,0,0   ; 03  spare
0006                          ENDIF      
0006   CF           RDROP:    RST   1   ; 06  drop the top of the return stack, then
0007   DF                     RST   3   ;     drop TOS (a spent flag) and go on
0008                VECS:        
0008                             ; ---- RST 1: rpop: pop the return stack into HL (DE is lost) -----------------
0008   2A 34 82     RPOP:     LHLD   RSP   ; 08
000B   5E                     MOV   E,M   
000C   23                     INX   H   
000D   56                     MOV   D,M   
000E   23                     INX   H   
000F   22 34 82               SHLD   RSP   
0012   EB                     XCHG      
0013   C9                     RET      ; 13  (so RST 2 is not used)
0014   EB           H_TOR:    XCHG      ; 14  "{" TOS to the return stack; rpushd
0015   C3 B3 00               JMP   rpushd   ;     brings up the new TOS
0018                             ; ---- RST 3: drop TOS, then next ---------------------------------------------
0018   D1           RST18:    POP   D   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0019   E1                     POP   H   ;     new TOS = NOS
001A   C3 31 00               JMP   next0   
001D   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   H   ; 1D  "}" return stack to TOS
001E   CF                     RST   1   
001F   F7                     RST   6   
0020                             ; ---- RST 4: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) ----------------------------------
0020   AF           NEG16:    XRA   A   ; 20
0021   95                     SUB   L   
0022   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0023   9F                     SBB   A   
0024   94                     SUB   H   
0025   67                     MOV   H,A   
0026   C9                     RET      
0027   E9           JPHL:     PCHL      ; 27  (for the machine-code call)
0028                             ; ---- RST 5: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL) --------------------------------
0028                RST28:       
0028                          IFN   CPM   
0028   C3 03 FF     PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B                          IF   CPM   
                              JMP   putc   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B                             ; exec: "`" with no hex digit after it: call the machine code at TOS. It
002B                             ; returns here, with its top cell on the stack: that becomes the new TOS.
002B   CD 27 00     EXEC:     CALL   jphl   ; 2B
002E   E1                     POP   H   
002F   F7                     RST   6   
0030                             ; ---- RST 6: next character --------------------------------------------------
0030   D1           RST30:    POP   D   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0031                          IF   CPM   
                              JMP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0031                          ENDIF      
0031                VECEND:      
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0031                             ; 
0031                             ;    00h          end of program
0031                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0031                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0031                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0031                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0031                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                NEXT0:       
0031                          IF   CHECKED   
0031   CD 86 03               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0034                          ENDIF      
0034   0A                     LDAX   B   
0035   03                     INX   B   
0036   D6 21                  SUI   21h   ; A = c - 21h
0038   DA 7A 00               JC   ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
003B   FE 0F                  CPI   0Fh   
003D   DA 6B 00               JC   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
0040   D6 0F                  SUI   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0042   FE 0A                  CPI   0Ah   
0044   DA 50 02               JC   digit   ; 30h-39h
0047   FE 11                  CPI   11h   
0049   DA 69 00               JC   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
004C   D6 11                  SUI   11h   ; A = c - 41h
004E   FE 1A                  CPI   1Ah   
0050   DA A9 00               JC   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
0053   FE 20                  CPI   20h   
0055   DA 67 00               JC   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0058   FE 3A                  CPI   3Ah   
005A   DA A3 00               JC   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
005D   FE 3E                  CPI   3Eh   
005F                          IF   CHECKED   
005F   CA 31 00               JZ   next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
0062   D2 D2 03               JNC   e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
0065                          ENDIF      
0065                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JNC   next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
0065                          ENDIF      
0065   D6 1A                  SUI   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
0067   D6 09        P5B:      SUI   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
0069   C6 05        P3A:      ADI   5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
006B                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
006B                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
006B   C6 30        PUNCT:    ADI   PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
006D   5F                     MOV   E,A   
006E   16 02                  MVI   D,PTAB / 256   
0070   FE 46                  CPI   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
0072   1A                     LDAX   D   
0073   5F                     MOV   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
0074                          IFN   CPM   
0074   3E 00                  MVI   A,0   
0076   17                     RAL      ; its page: 0 + carry
0077                          ENDIF      
0077                          IF   CPM   
                              MVI   A,1   
                              ACI   0   ; its page: 1 + carry
0077                          ENDIF      
0077   57                     MOV   D,A   
0078   D5                     PUSH   D   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
0079   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
007A                             ; ctl: characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
007A   C6 21        CTL:      ADI   21h   ; back to c; zero only for NUL
007C   C2 31 00               JNZ   next0   ; the rest are ignored
007F   C3 09 FF     ENDPROG:   JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
0082                             ; =============================================================================
0082                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0082                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.)
0082                             ; =============================================================================
0082   D1           H_XOR:    POP   D   
0083   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0084   AA                     XRA   D   
0085   67                     MOV   H,A   
0086   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0087   AB                     XRA   E   
0088   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0089   F7                     RST   6   
008A   D1           H_OR:     POP   D   
008B   7C                     MOV   A,H   
008C   B2                     ORA   D   
008D   67                     MOV   H,A   
008E   7D                     MOV   A,L   
008F   B3                     ORA   E   
0090   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0091   F7                     RST   6   
0092   E7           H_NOT:    RST   4   ; ~x = -x - 1
0093   2B                     DCX   H   
0094   F7                     RST   6   
0095                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0095                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0095   EB           H_ALLOC:   XCHG      
0096   2A 7C 82               LHLD   HEAP   
0099   E5                     PUSH   H   
009A   19                     DAD   D   ; the new top
009B                          IF   CHECKED   
009B   CD 47 03               CALL   chkhp   
009E                          ENDIF      
009E   22 7C 82               SHLD   HEAP   
00A1   E1                     POP   H   
00A2   F7                     RST   6   
00A3                             ; ---- the letters and digits --------------------------------------------------
00A3                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
00A3   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   H   
00A4   87                     ADD   A   
00A5   6F                     MOV   L,A   
00A6   26 82                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   
00A8   F7                     RST   6   
00A9                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
00A9                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
00A9   E5           UPPER:    PUSH   H   ; keep TOS: rpushd pops it back
00AA   87                     ADD   A   
00AB   6F                     MOV   L,A   
00AC   26 82                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
00AE   50                     MOV   D,B   
00AF   59                     MOV   E,C   ; DE = the return address
00B0   4E                     MOV   C,M   
00B1   23                     INX   H   
00B2   46                     MOV   B,M   ; IP = the word's body, and fall into rpushd
00B3                             ; rpushd: push DE on the return stack, then pop TOS off the data stack and
00B3                             ; go on. Every push of the return stack ends here: for a word call the cell
00B3                             ; popped is the TOS that upper parked; for "(" and "{" it is the cell under
00B3                             ; the one that was used up.
00B3                RPUSHD:      
00B3                          IF   CHECKED   
00B3   CD BD 03               CALL   chkbrk   ; Ctrl-C is checked at every word call, block
00B6                          ENDIF      ;   entry, loop-back and "{"
00B6   2A 34 82               LHLD   RSP   
00B9   2B                     DCX   H   
00BA   72                     MOV   M,D   
00BB   2B                     DCX   H   
00BC   73                     MOV   M,E   
00BD   22 34 82               SHLD   RSP   
00C0   E1                     POP   H   
00C1   F7                     RST   6   
00C2                             ; ---- machine code: the grave -----------------------------------------------
00C2                             ; "`" plus a hex digit loads bytes: ( addr -- addr' ). Pairs of hex digits
00C2                             ; are stored from addr until a non-hex character; then a RET (C9h) is
00C2                             ; written and its address is left. An odd last digit is consumed and dropped.
00C2                             ; "`" plus anything else calls the machine code at TOS: ( addr -- ). The
00C2                             ; code is entered by CALL with the data stack above the return address; it
00C2                             ; must keep BC, and on return the top cell becomes the new TOS.
00C2   CD 17 03     H_GRAVE:   CALL   hexc   
00C5   D2 2B 00               JNC   exec   
00C8   87           HX1:      ADD   A   
00C9   87                     ADD   A   
00CA   87                     ADD   A   
00CB   87                     ADD   A   
00CC   57                     MOV   D,A   ; the high digit
00CD   CD 17 03               CALL   hexc   
00D0   D2 DC 00               JNC   hx2   ; odd digit: consumed and dropped
00D3   B2                     ORA   D   
00D4   77                     MOV   M,A   
00D5   23                     INX   H   
00D6   CD 17 03               CALL   hexc   
00D9   DA C8 00               JC   hx1   
00DC   36 C9        HX2:      MVI   M,0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
00DE   F7                     RST   6   
00DF                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
00DF                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
00DF                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
00DF                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
00DF                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
00DF                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. TOS is parked on the stack
00DF                             ; while rpop uses HL, and the drop at the end brings it back.
00DF   E5           H_RET:    PUSH   H   
00E0   CF           RET2:     RST   1   
00E1   44                     MOV   B,H   
00E2   4D                     MOV   C,L   
00E3   DF                     RST   3   
00E4                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
00E4                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
00E4                             ; The flag stays in HL as the spent cell that rdrop and ret2 drop.
00E4   7C           H_BREAK:   MOV   A,H   
00E5   B5                     ORA   L   
00E6   CA D1 01               JZ   h_drop   ; false: just drop the flag
00E9   CD C0 02               CALL   skip   
00EC   B7                     ORA   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
00ED   C2 E0 00               JNZ   ret2   
00F0   C3 06 00               JMP   rdrop   
00F3                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
00F3                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
00F3                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
00F3                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
00F3                             ; checked build stops on it.)
00F3   0A           H_DEF:    LDAX   B   
00F4   03                     INX   B   
00F5   D6 41                  SUI   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
00F7   5F                     MOV   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
00F8   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   ; fold case
00FA   FE 1A                  CPI   26   
00FC   D2 0C 01               JNC   def2   ; not a letter
00FF   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0100   87                     ADD   A   
0101   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0102   16 82                  MVI   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
0104   79                     MOV   A,C   
0105   12                     STAX   D   
0106   1C                     INR   E   
0107   78                     MOV   A,B   
0108   12                     STAX   D   
0109   C3 15 01               JMP   skipnx   
010C                DEF2:        
010C                          IF   CHECKED   
010C   7B                     MOV   A,E   
010D   FE DF                  CPI   " "-"A"+256   
010F   C2 EC 03               JNZ   e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0112                          ENDIF      
0112   E5                     PUSH   H   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0113   60                     MOV   H,B   
0114   69                     MOV   L,C   
0115                SKIPNX:      
0115                          IF   CHECKED   
0115   0B                     DCX   B   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
0116                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
0116   CD C0 02     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
0119   F7                     RST   6   
011A   5E           H_FETCH:   MOV   E,M   ; "@"
011B   23                     INX   H   
011C   56                     MOV   D,M   
011D   EB                     XCHG      
011E   F7                     RST   6   
011F                             ; =============================================================================
011F                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
011F                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it in the unchecked build), so its long
011F                             ;  tail may run past that page.
011F                             ; =============================================================================
011F                             ; ---- flow control ----------------------------------------------------------
011F                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
011F                             ; the matching ")".
011F   7C           H_OPEN:   MOV   A,H   
0120   B5                     ORA   L   
0121   E1                     POP   H   
0122   CA 16 01               JZ   skipo   
0125   E5                     PUSH   H   ; (rpushd pops it again)
0126   50                     MOV   D,B   
0127   59                     MOV   E,C   ; the block starts at the IP
0128   C3 B3 00               JMP   rpushd   
012B                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
012B                             ; drops it and carries on.
012B   7C           H_CLOSE:   MOV   A,H   
012C   B5                     ORA   L   
012D   CA 06 00               JZ   rdrop   
0130   CF                     RST   1   ; pop the block start ...
0131   44                     MOV   B,H   
0132   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; ... jump to it ...
0133   EB                     XCHG      
0134   C3 B3 00               JMP   rpushd   ; ... and push it back (which drops the flag)
0137                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0137                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0137   0A           H_SUB:    LDAX   B   
0138   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
013A   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
013C   DA 56 02               JC   negnum   
013F   E7                     RST   4   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
0140   D1           H_ADD:    POP   D   
0141   19                     DAD   D   
0142   F7                     RST   6   
0143   D1           H_AND:    POP   D   
0144   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0145   A2                     ANA   D   
0146   67                     MOV   H,A   
0147   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0148   A3                     ANA   E   
0149   6F                     MOV   L,A   
014A   F7                     RST   6   
014B                             ; Signed compares. Both are "DE < HL" for the right pair: > swaps the two
014B                             ; cells first (XTHL), < doesn't. There is no overflow flag, so the signed
014B                             ; answer is the unsigned borrow of DE - HL, flipped when the signs differ.
014B                             ; SBB A turns a carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
014B   E3           H_GT:     XTHL      ; a > b  is  b < a
014C   D1           H_LT:     POP   D   ; a < b: DE = a, HL = b
014D   7B                     MOV   A,E   
014E   95                     SUB   L   
014F   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0150   9C                     SBB   H   
0151   9F                     SBB   A   ; A = -1 if DE < HL unsigned
0152   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0153   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0154   AA                     XRA   D   
0155   17                     RAL      ; carry = the signs differ
0156   9F                     SBB   A   
0157   AD                     XRA   L   ; flip when they do
0158   67                     MOV   H,A   
0159   6F                     MOV   L,A   
015A   F7                     RST   6   
015B   D1           H_EQ:     POP   D   
015C   7D                     MOV   A,L   
015D   AB                     XRA   E   
015E   6F                     MOV   L,A   
015F   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0160   AA                     XRA   D   
0161   B5                     ORA   L   ; zero if equal
0162   D6 01                  SUI   1   ; carry only for zero
0164   9F                     SBB   A   
0165   67                     MOV   H,A   
0166   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0167   F7                     RST   6   
0168                             ; "*": shift-and-add on the multiplier's low bit, so it stops as soon as the
0168                             ; multiplier is used up; only the low 16 bits are kept.
0168   D1           H_MUL:    POP   D   ; DE = multiplicand
0169   C5                     PUSH   B   
016A   44                     MOV   B,H   
016B   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; BC = multiplier
016C   21 00 00               LXI   H,0   
016F   78           MUL1:     MOV   A,B   
0170   B7                     ORA   A   ; clear carry
0171   1F                     RAR      
0172   47                     MOV   B,A   
0173   79                     MOV   A,C   
0174   1F                     RAR      
0175   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; BC >> 1, carry = the bit shifted out
0176   D2 7A 01               JNC   mul2   
0179   19                     DAD   D   
017A   EB           MUL2:     XCHG      
017B   29                     DAD   H   ; multiplicand << 1
017C   EB                     XCHG      
017D   78                     MOV   A,B   
017E   B1                     ORA   C   
017F   C2 6F 01               JNZ   mul1   
0182   C1                     POP   B   
0183   F7                     RST   6   
0184                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
0184                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
0184                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
0184                             ; stops on it.
0184                H_DIV:       
0184                          IF   CHECKED   
0184   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0185   B5                     ORA   L   
0186   CA E9 03               JZ   e_zero   
0189                          ENDIF      
0189   D1                     POP   D   ; DE = a, HL = b
018A   C5                     PUSH   B   
018B   7A                     MOV   A,D   
018C   B7                     ORA   A   
018D   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of a (for r)
018E   AC                     XRA   H   
018F   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of q
0190   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0191   B7                     ORA   A   
0192   FC 20 00               CM   neg16   ; HL = |b|
0195   EB                     XCHG      
0196   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0197   B7                     ORA   A   
0198   FC 20 00               CM   neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
019B   CD 73 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, BC = r
019E   F1                     POP   PSW   
019F   FC 20 00               CM   neg16   ; q's sign
01A2   EB                     XCHG      ; DE = q
01A3   60                     MOV   H,B   
01A4   69                     MOV   L,C   ; HL = r
01A5   F1                     POP   PSW   
01A6   FC 20 00               CM   neg16   ; r's sign
01A9   C1                     POP   B   
01AA   D5                     PUSH   D   ; q under r
01AB   F7                     RST   6   
01AC                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
01AC   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   H   ; ":"
01AD   F7                     RST   6   
01AE   E3           H_SWAP:   XTHL      ; "%"
01AF   F7                     RST   6   
01B0                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
01B0                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
01B0                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
01B0                          IF   CHECKED   
01B0   CD 37 03               CALL   chkst   
01B3                          ENDIF      
01B3   D1                     POP   D   
01B4   73                     MOV   M,E   
01B5   23                     INX   H   
01B6   72                     MOV   M,D   
01B7   DF                     RST   3   
01B8                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
01B8                          IF   CHECKED   
01B8   CD 37 03               CALL   chkst   
01BB                          ENDIF      
01BB   D1                     POP   D   
01BC   73                     MOV   M,E   
01BD   DF                     RST   3   
01BE                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
01BE                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
01BE   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   H   
01BF   60                     MOV   H,B   
01C0   69                     MOV   L,C   
01C1   CD 04 03               CALL   skipstr   
01C4                          IF   CHECKED   
01C4   B7                     ORA   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
01C5   CA E1 03               JZ   e_quote   
01C8                          ENDIF      
01C8   F7                     RST   6   
01C9                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
01C9                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
01C9                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
01C9                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_PRINT:   MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              CPI   22h   
                              JZ   h_drop   
                              CPI   "/"   
                              JNZ   pr1   
                              MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              ANI   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   5   
                              JMP   h_print   
01C9                          ENDIF      
01C9                          IF   CHECKED   
01C9                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
01C9                             ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
01C9                             ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
01C9   E5           H_PRINT:   PUSH   H   
01CA   CD 5D 03               CALL   prstr   
01CD   D1                     POP   D   
01CE   DF                     RST   3   
01CF                          ENDIF      
01CF   7D           H_EMIT:   MOV   A,L   ; "'"
01D0   EF                     RST   5   
01D1   DF           H_DROP:   RST   3   ; ";" is this one byte
01D2                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
01D2   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   B   
01D3   CD A5 02               CALL   psgn   
01D6   C1                     POP   B   
01D7   DF                     RST   3   
01D8                          IF   CHECKED   ; (the checked build has no room to start ","
01D8   6E           H_CFETCH:   MOV   L,M   ;   as late as the unchecked one does: see
01D9   26 00                  MVI   H,0   ;   the end of "?")
01DB   F7                     RST   6   
01DC                          ENDIF      
01DC                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
01DC                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
01DC                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
01DC                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
01DC                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
01DC   7C           H_KEY:    MOV   A,H   
01DD   B7                     ORA   A   
01DE   FA FC 01               JM   line   
01E1   1E 28        KT1:      MVI   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
01E3   CD 2A 03     KT2:      CALL   getk   
01E6   C2 F8 01               JNZ   kt3   
01E9   1D                     DCR   E   
01EA   C2 E3 01               JNZ   kt2   
01ED   7C                     MOV   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
01EE   B5                     ORA   L   
01EF   CA E1 01               JZ   kt1   
01F2   2B                     DCX   H   
01F3   7C                     MOV   A,H   
01F4   B5                     ORA   L   
01F5   C2 E1 01               JNZ   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
01F8                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              DB   0FEh   ; (CPI: steps over the one byte of ",")
                    H_CFETCH:   MOV   A,M   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
01F8                          ENDIF      
01F8   6F           KT3:      MOV   L,A   
01F9   26 00                  MVI   H,0   
01FB   F7                     RST   6   
01FC                          IF   CPM   
                                 ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
                                 ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
                    LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBB   A   
                              ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              XRI   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
                              STA   LBHDR   
                              PUSH   B   
                              LXI   D,LBHDR   
                              MVI   C,10   
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              POP   B   
                              LXI   H,LBHDR+1   
                              MOV   A,M   ; the count typed (0-127)
                              INR   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
                              ADD   L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
                              MOV   L,A   
                              MVI   M,13   
                              MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
                              RST   6   
01FC                          ENDIF      
01FC                          IFN   CPM   
01FC                             ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
01FC                             ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
01FC                             ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
01FC                             ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
01FC                             ; a full line.
01FC   11 7F 00     LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
01FF   19                     DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
0200   9F                     SBB   A   
0201   A5                     ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
0202   2F                     CMA      
0203   57                     MOV   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
0204                             ;   at most
0204   21 80 82               LXI   H,LINEBUF   
0207   CD 2A 03     LN2:      CALL   getk   
020A   CA 07 02               JZ   ln2   
020D   FE 0D                  CPI   13   
020F   CA 2C 02               JZ   ln5   
0212   FE 08                  CPI   8   
0214   CA 24 02               JZ   ln4   
0217   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0218   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0219   BA                     CMP   D   
021A   CA 07 02               JZ   ln2   ; full
021D   73                     MOV   M,E   
021E   2C                     INR   L   
021F   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0220   EF           LN3:      RST   5   
0221   C3 07 02               JMP   ln2   
0224   2D           LN4:      DCR   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
0225   FA 20 02               JM   ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
0228   2C                     INR   L   ;   upper half of the page)
0229   C3 07 02               JMP   ln2   
022C   77           LN5:      MOV   M,A   ; the CR
022D   2E 80                  MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
022F   F7                     RST   6   
0230                          ENDIF      
0230                             ; =============================================================================
0230                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order.
0230                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
0230                             ; =============================================================================
0230                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
0230                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
0230                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
0230                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
0230                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
0230                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
0230                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
0230                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
0230                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
0230   B0           PTAB:     DB   h_store & 0FFh   ; !
0231   BE                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   ; "
0232   D2                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   ; #
0233   C9                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   ; $
0234   AE                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
0235   43                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   ; &
0236   CF                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0237   1F                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0238   2B                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   ; )
0239   68                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   ; *
023A   40                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   ; +
023B   D8                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   ; ,
023C   37                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   ; -
023D   B8                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   ; .
023E   84                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   ; /
023F   AC                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   ; :
0240   D1                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
0241   4C                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   ; <
0242   5B                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   ; =
0243   4B                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   ; >
0244   DC                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   ; ?
0245   1A                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   ; @
0246   F3                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   ; [
0247   E4                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   ; \
0248   DF                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   ; ]
0249   82                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   ; ^
024A   95                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   ; _
024B   C2                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   ; `
024C   14                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   ; {
024D   8A                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   ; |
024E   1D                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   ; }
024F   92                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   ; ~
0250                PTABEND:      
0250                             ; =============================================================================
0250                             ;  Routines (no handler starts past this point)
0250                             ; =============================================================================
0250                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
0250   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   H   
0251   0B                     DCX   B   
0252   CD 5C 02               CALL   rdnum   
0255   F7                     RST   6   
0256                             ; negnum: "-" directly before a digit: read the number, negate it.
0256   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   H   
0257   CD 5C 02               CALL   rdnum   
025A   E7                     RST   4   
025B   F7                     RST   6   
025C                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
025C                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
025C   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LXI   H,0   
025F   0A           RDN1:     LDAX   B   
0260   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
0262   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
0264   D0                     RNC      
0265   03                     INX   B   
0266   54                     MOV   D,H   
0267   5D                     MOV   E,L   
0268   29                     DAD   H   
0269   29                     DAD   H   
026A   19                     DAD   D   
026B   29                     DAD   H   ; HL * 10
026C   5F                     MOV   E,A   
026D   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
026F   19                     DAD   D   
0270   C3 5F 02               JMP   rdn1   
0273                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, BC = remainder.
0273                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. HL holds the dividend and, as its bits
0273                             ; leave at the top, the quotient bits arrive at the bottom. The loop counter
0273                             ; lives on the stack, since A is busy with the shifts.
0273                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
0273   01 00 00     UDIV:     LXI   B,0   
0276   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0277   EE 02                  XRI   2   
0279   B2                     ORA   D   
027A   C2 87 02               JNZ   udv0   
027D   B4                     ORA   H   ; A was 0, and the carry is clear
027E   1F                     RAR      
027F   67                     MOV   H,A   
0280   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0281   1F                     RAR      
0282   6F                     MOV   L,A   ; the quotient
0283   78                     MOV   A,B   
0284   17                     RAL      
0285   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out
0286   C9                     RET      
0287   3E 10        UDV0:     MVI   A,16   
0289   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
028A   29           UDV1:     DAD   H   ; next dividend bit into the carry
028B   79                     MOV   A,C   
028C   17                     RAL      
028D   4F                     MOV   C,A   
028E   78                     MOV   A,B   
028F   17                     RAL      
0290   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC = BC*2 + bit
0291   79                     MOV   A,C   
0292   93                     SUB   E   
0293   78                     MOV   A,B   
0294   9A                     SBB   D   ; carry if BC < DE
0295   DA 9D 02               JC   udv2   
0298   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC - DE (high byte; A holds it)
0299   79                     MOV   A,C   
029A   93                     SUB   E   
029B   4F                     MOV   C,A   
029C   2C                     INR   L   ; quotient bit
029D   F1           UDV2:     POP   PSW   
029E   3D                     DCR   A   
029F   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
02A0   C2 8A 02               JNZ   udv1   
02A3   F1                     POP   PSW   
02A4   C9                     RET      
02A5                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
02A5   7C           PSGN:     MOV   A,H   
02A6   B7                     ORA   A   
02A7   F2 AE 02               JP   pdec   
02AA   3E 2D                  MVI   A,"-"   
02AC   EF                     RST   5   
02AD   E7                     RST   4   
02AE                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
02AE                             ; Uses BC.
02AE   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LXI   D,10   
02B1   CD 73 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, C = the last digit
02B4   79                     MOV   A,C   
02B5   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
02B6   7C                     MOV   A,H   
02B7   B5                     ORA   L   
02B8   C4 AE 02               CNZ   pdec   
02BB   F1                     POP   PSW   
02BC   C6 30                  ADI   "0"   
02BE   EF                     RST   5   
02BF   C9                     RET      
02C0                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
02C0                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
02C0                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
02C0                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
02C0                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
02C0                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INR that an opener comes back to.
02C0                             ; 
02C0                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
02C0                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
02C0                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
02C0                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. The place where
02C0                             ; the skip started is kept on the stack, for the report.
02C0                SKIP:        
02C0                          IF   CHECKED   
02C0   C5                     PUSH   B   
02C1   0B                     DCX   B   
02C2   0A                     LDAX   B   
02C3   03                     INX   B   
02C4   5F                     MOV   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
02C5                          ENDIF      
02C5   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
02C7   14           SK3:      INR   D   ; an opener: one deeper
02C8   0A           SK1:      LDAX   B   
02C9                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              INX   B   
                              ORA   A   
                              JZ   endprog   
02C9                          ENDIF      
02C9                          IF   CHECKED   
02C9   B7                     ORA   A   
02CA   CA F8 02               JZ   sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
02CD   03                     INX   B   
02CE                          ENDIF      
02CE   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
02D0   CC 04 03               CZ   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
02D3   D6 28                  SUI   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
02D5   CA C7 02               JZ   sk3   
02D8   3D                     DCR   A   ; ")"
02D9   CA E6 02               JZ   sk4   
02DC   D6 32                  SUI   "["-")"   
02DE   CA C7 02               JZ   sk3   
02E1   FE 02                  CPI   "]"-"["   
02E3   C2 C8 02               JNZ   sk1   
02E6   15           SK4:      DCR   D   
02E7                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RZ      ; the closer at this level
                              JMP   sk1   
02E7                          ENDIF      
02E7                          IF   CHECKED   
02E7   C2 C8 02               JNZ   sk1   
02EA   57                     MOV   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
02EB   AB                     XRA   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
02EC   E6 06                  ANI   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
02EE   FE 02                  CPI   2   ;   closer, and only then
02F0   7A                     MOV   A,D   
02F1   D1                     POP   D   ; (where the skip started)
02F2   C0                     RNZ      
02F3   42                     MOV   B,D   ; N. The place is the opener
02F4   4B                     MOV   C,E   
02F5   C3 FF 02               JMP   sk7   
02F8   7B           SK6:      MOV   A,E   ; the text ran out:
02F9   E6 04                  ANI   4   
02FB   C2 7F 00               JNZ   endprog   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
02FE   C1                     POP   B   
02FF   3E 4E        SK7:      MVI   A,"N"   
0301   C3 EF 03               JMP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
0304                          ENDIF      
0304                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
0304                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
0304                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SS0:      INX   B   
                    SKIPSTR:   LDAX   B   
                              INX   B   
                              CPI   "/"   
                              JZ   ss0   
                              CPI   22h   
                              JNZ   skipstr   
                              RET      
0304                          ENDIF      
0304                          IF   CHECKED   
0304                             ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
0304                             ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
0304   0A           SKIPSTR:   LDAX   B   
0305   B7                     ORA   A   
0306   C8                     RZ      
0307   03                     INX   B   
0308   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
030A   C8                     RZ      
030B   FE 2F                  CPI   "/"   
030D   C2 04 03               JNZ   skipstr   
0310   0A                     LDAX   B   ; the escaped character
0311   B7                     ORA   A   
0312   C8                     RZ      
0313   03                     INX   B   
0314   C3 04 03               JMP   skipstr   
0317                          ENDIF      
0317                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
0317                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
0317                             ; return with the carry clear.
0317   0A           HEXC:     LDAX   B   
0318   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
031A   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
031C   DA 28 03               JC   hc1   
031F   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   
0321   D6 11                  SUI   11h   
0323   FE 06                  CPI   6   
0325   D0                     RNC      
0326   D6 F6                  SUI   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
0328   03           HC1:      INX   B   
0329   C9                     RET      
032A                             ; =============================================================================
032A                             ;  Console layer: getk returns a waiting key in A (zero flag clear), or
032A                             ;  A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc (RST 5) prints A.
032A                             ;  Both keep BC, DE and HL. In the generic build they are the host's KEY and
032A                             ;  CONOUT routines themselves.
032A                             ; =============================================================================
032A                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-CHECKED)   
                    GETK:     EQU   KEY   ; the host's routine does the whole job
032A                          ENDIF      
032A                          IF   CHECKED   
032A   E5           GETK:     PUSH   H   ; a key held back by the break check goes
032B   21 36 82               LXI   H,KEYBUF   ;   first, and is taken out of the buffer
032E   7E                     MOV   A,M   
032F   36 00                  MVI   M,0   
0331   E1                     POP   H   
0332   B7                     ORA   A   
0333   C0                     RNZ      
0334                          ENDIF      
0334                          IF   (1-CPM)*CHECKED   
0334   C3 06 FF               JMP   KEY   
0337                          ENDIF      
0337                          IF   CPM*(1-CHECKED)   
                    GETK:        
0337                          ENDIF      
0337                          IF   CPM   
                              MVI   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
                                 ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
                                 ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
                    PUTC:     PUSH   B   
                              PUSH   D   
                              PUSH   H   
                              MOV   E,A   
                              MVI   C,6   
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              POP   H   
                              POP   D   
                              POP   B   
                              ORA   A   ; (for getk)
                              RET      
0337                          ENDIF      
0337                             ; =============================================================================
0337                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
0337                             ; =============================================================================
0337                          IF   CHECKED   
0337                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
0337                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
0337                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
0337                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
0337                             ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
0337                             ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
0337                             ; Keeps HL and BC.
0337   23           CHKST:    INX   H   
0338   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0339   2B                     DCX   H   
033A   FE 82                  CPI   LETPAGE   
033C   DA 42 03               JC   e_store   
033F                          ENDIF      
033F                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
033F   FE F0                  CPI   HEAPLIM   
0341   D8                     RC      
0342                          ENDIF      
0342                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              MOV   E,A   
                              LDA   0007h   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
                              DCR   A   
                              CMP   E   
                              RNC      
0342                          ENDIF      
0342                          IF   CHECKED   
0342   3E 4F        E_STORE:   MVI   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
0344   C3 EF 03               JMP   errp   
0347                             ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the count, the carry is from adding
0347                             ; it, and the old top is on the stack under the return address. Stop if the
0347                             ; new top is not below the limit page, or is below the program's end.
0347                CHKHP:       
0347                          ENDIF      
0347                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                                 ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
                                 ; range, so the add is tested too: growing must not carry, and
                                 ; releasing must.
                              MOV   A,D   
                              RAR      ; the carry comes in above the count's sign:
                              ADI   40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
                              ADD   A   
                              JC   e_heap   
                              LDA   0007h   
                              DCR   A   
                              CMP   H   
                              JC   e_heap   
0347                          ENDIF      
0347                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
0347                             ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
0347                             ; round always falls outside it.)
0347   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0348   FE F0                  CPI   HEAPLIM   
034A   D2 56 03               JNC   e_heap   
034D                          ENDIF      
034D                          IF   CHECKED   
034D   EB                     XCHG      
034E   E5                     PUSH   H   ; the count
034F   2A 38 82               LHLD   NPEND   
0352   19                     DAD   D   ; carry: at or above the program's end
0353   E1                     POP   H   
0354   EB                     XCHG      
0355   D8                     RC      
0356   EB           E_HEAP:   XCHG      ; put the count back in TOS for the report,
0357   D1                     POP   D   ;   and drop the return address and the old
0358   3E 48                  MVI   A,"H"   ;   top
035A   C3 EF 03               JMP   errp   
035D                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
035D                             ; "$", and the error report's texts). A NUL first is an error: Q.
035D   7E           PRSTR:    MOV   A,M   
035E   23                     INX   H   
035F   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
0361   C8                     RZ      
0362   B7                     ORA   A   
0363   CA 73 03               JZ   e_dollar   
0366   FE 2F                  CPI   "/"   
0368   C2 6F 03               JNZ   prs1   
036B   7E                     MOV   A,M   
036C   23                     INX   H   
036D   E6 BF                  ANI   0BFh   
036F   EF           PRS1:     RST   5   
0370   C3 5D 03               JMP   prstr   
0373   D1           E_DOLLAR:   POP   D   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop the return address,
0374   E1                     POP   H   ;   and put the string's address back in TOS
0375   3E 51                  MVI   A,"Q"   
0377   C3 F0 03               JMP   error   
037A                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
037A                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
037A   3E 0D        PNL:      MVI   A,13   
037C   EF                     RST   5   
037D   3E 0A                  MVI   A,10   
037F   EF                     RST   5   
0380   E3           PMSG:     XTHL      
0381   CD 5D 03               CALL   prstr   
0384   E3                     XTHL      
0385   C9                     RET      
0386                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
0386                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
0386                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
0386                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
0386                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
0386                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile.
0386   EB           CHKSTK:   XCHG      ; DE = TOS (HL is needed for the pointers)
0387   21 05 7E               LXI   H,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
038A   39                     DAD   SP   
038B   DA B5 03               JC   e_under   
038E   24                     INR   H   
038F   C2 AF 03               JNZ   e_over   
0392   2A 34 82               LHLD   RSP   ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
0395   7C                     MOV   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
0396   FE 80                  CPI   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
0398   C2 AC 03               JNZ   e_rover   ;   page, in the guard band)
039B   7D                     MOV   A,L   
039C   FE E1                  CPI   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
039E   D2 A3 03               JNC   e_runder   
03A1   EB                     XCHG      ; TOS back
03A2   C9                     RET      
03A3   21 E0 80     E_RUNDER:   LXI   H,RSTOP   ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
03A6   22 34 82               SHLD   RSP   
03A9   3E 72                  MVI   A,"r"   
03AB   21                     DB   21h   ; (LXI H hides the next entry; HL is free)
03AC   3E 52        E_ROVER:   MVI   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
03AE   21                     DB   21h   
03AF   3E 53        E_OVER:   MVI   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
03B1   EB                     XCHG      ; TOS back
03B2   C3 EF 03               JMP   errp   
03B5   31 FC 81     E_UNDER:   LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
03B8   3E 73                  MVI   A,"s"   
03BA   C3 F0 03               JMP   error   
03BD                             ; chkbrk: a waiting key is read now; Ctrl-C stops the program, anything
03BD                             ; else is held for the next "?". Keeps BC, DE, HL.
03BD   CD 2A 03     CHKBRK:   CALL   getk   
03C0   C8                     RZ      
03C1   FE 03                  CPI   3   
03C3   32 36 82               STA   KEYBUF   
03C6   C0                     RNZ      
03C7   AF                     XRA   A   
03C8   32 36 82               STA   KEYBUF   
03CB   D1                     POP   D   ; Ctrl-C. Drop the return address; the cell on
03CC   E1                     POP   H   ;   top of the stack is the TOS that rpushd
03CD   3E 42                  MVI   A,"B"   ;   was about to bring back
03CF   C3 F0 03               JMP   error   
03D2                             ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
03D2                             ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a JMP, C3h, in
03D2                             ; every build: if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of an undefined
03D2                             ; word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
03D2   04           E_HI:     INR   B   
03D3   05                     DCR   B   
03D4   C2 E6 03               JNZ   e_resv   
03D7   E5                     PUSH   H   
03D8   CF                     RST   1   
03D9   44                     MOV   B,H   
03DA   4D                     MOV   C,L   
03DB   E1                     POP   H   
03DC   3E 55                  MVI   A,"U"   
03DE   C3 F0 03               JMP   error   
03E1                             ; Error entries. Each loads its letter and then hides the next entry inside
03E1                             ; a 3-byte LXI D (the 11h), so they all fall through to `error`.
03E1   44           E_QUOTE:   MOV   B,H   ; an unclosed string: HL is its address, one
03E2   4D                     MOV   C,L   ;   past the opening quote, which is the place
03E3   3E 51                  MVI   A,"Q"   
03E5   11                     DB   11h   
03E6   3E 58        E_RESV:   MVI   A,"X"   ; a reserved byte outside a string
03E8   11                     DB   11h   
03E9   3E 5A        E_ZERO:   MVI   A,"Z"   ; dividing by zero
03EB   11                     DB   11h   
03EC   3E 57        E_BRACK:   MVI   A,"W"   ; bad character after [
03EE   FE                     DB   0FEh   ; (CPI hides the one byte of errp)
03EF                             ; errp: an error found inside a routine: drop its return address first.
03EF   D1           ERRP:     POP   D   
03F0                             ; error: the report, then the end. A = the letter, BC = one past the place,
03F0                             ; HL = TOS, and both stacks as the report is to show them:
03F0                             ; 
03F0                             ;   Err X @ line,col
03F0                             ;   up to 16 characters of the text from the place
03F0                             ;   Stk n: the top 8 cells at most, bottom to top
03F0                             ;   Rtn n
03F0   E5           ERROR:    PUSH   H   ; now the whole data stack is in memory
03F1   5F                     MOV   E,A   
03F2   CD 7A 03               CALL   pnl   
03F5   45 72 72 20 22         DB   "Err ",22h   
03FA   7B                     MOV   A,E   
03FB   EF                     RST   5   
03FC   CD 80 03               CALL   pmsg   
03FF   20 40 20 22            DB   " @ ",22h   
0403   0B                     DCX   B   ; BC = the place
0404                             ; The line and column. A place below the program is in the line
0404                             ; buffer: line 0. Otherwise count the LFs from the program's start;
0404                             ; DE = the line's number, HL = where it starts.
0404   21 80 82               LXI   H,LINEBUF   
0407   11 00 00               LXI   D,0   
040A   78                     MOV   A,B   
040B   FE 83                  CPI   PROG/256   
040D   DA 27 04               JC   er3   
0410   24                     INR   H   
0411   6B                     MOV   L,E   ; HL = PROG
0412   13           ER1:      INX   D   ; a new line starts at HL
0413   E5                     PUSH   H   
0414   7D           ER2:      MOV   A,L   
0415   91                     SUB   C   
0416   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0417   98                     SBB   B   
0418   D2 26 04               JNC   er2x   ; reached the place
041B   7E                     MOV   A,M   
041C   23                     INX   H   
041D   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
041F   C2 14 04               JNZ   er2   
0422   F1                     POP   PSW   
0423   C3 12 04               JMP   er1   
0426   E1           ER2X:     POP   H   
0427   C5           ER3:      PUSH   B   
0428   E5                     PUSH   H   
0429   EB                     XCHG      
042A   CD AE 02               CALL   pdec   ; the line
042D   3E 2C                  MVI   A,","   
042F   EF                     RST   5   
